
==============================================================================
Combining shards
==============================================================================
  discover_shard_0.json: 30 reference, 60 candidates, ligands a8ae9075598df11d, curation da70584f5064c941

Pooled: 30 reference actives, 60 candidates, 104 CPU-minutes

==============================================================================
How generation was constrained
==============================================================================
  anchoring motif(s), measured from the actives: amidine
  fragment pool: 26 carrying the motif, used as build seeds; 55 motif-free, used as reagents. Every product therefore grows from exactly one warhead by construction rather than being filtered afterwards -- the filter version spends the generation budget on artefacts, which is how a previous run reached 15 artefacts and an empty shortlist.

==============================================================================
The feature profile the candidates were judged against
==============================================================================
  built from 30 actives against 1200 background compounds
  background: unrelated ChEMBL targets (presumed non-binders)
    families: protein kinase (360), aminergic GPCR (240), nuclear receptor (240), carbonic anhydrase (120), peptide GPCR (120), oxidoreductase (120)
  conserved: amidine, basic_nitrogen_any, halogen_on_aromatic, primary_aliphatic_amine
  most discriminating: amidine
  set aside as ubiquitous: aromatic_ring

  prevalence (actives vs background):
    amidine: 90% vs 4% (22.5x)

  CAUTION: a feature can be enriched among potent compounds without
  being what binds. Late-stage optimisation adds fluorine, so aromatic
  halogens correlate with potency inside an optimised series while
  forming no specific interaction. This profile measures correlation
  with potency, not binding mechanism, and cannot tell the two apart.

==============================================================================
4. Triage against the reference distribution
==============================================================================
  reference actives by raw score: median -9.03, range -10.20 to -7.51 kcal/mol
  reference actives by ligand efficiency: median -0.261, range -0.347 to -0.149 kcal/mol/atom

  TRIAGE WITHHELD. 22 of 60 candidates reach a ligand efficiency of -0.261 kcal/mol/atom, the median known active -- but not one of them reaches it by more than Vina's own 2.5 kcal/mol method error (margins median 0.49, max 1.17 kcal/mol).
  So the cut runs through a part of the distribution narrower than the method can resolve. Those candidates are indistinguishable from a median known active at Vina's precision, and so are most of the 38 above the line. A subset called 'passing' would report as a filter something that does not filter.
  All 60 candidates are reported below with their efficiencies, unranked and uncut. The threshold stays a stated reference point.

  ligand efficiency across survivors: -0.290 to -0.155 kcal/mol/atom

  NOT RANKED, and not a shortlist. The triage was withheld above, so these are reported in the order they were docked. Sorting them by ligand efficiency would imply an ordering the method cannot support: the whole set spans less than Vina's error, so the first entry is not better evidence than the last.

