==============================================================================
What these are, and what they are not
==============================================================================
These structures have NO predicted potency. Generated candidates sit
outside the QSAR model's applicability domain almost by construction --
the reason to generate them is that they are new, and new is exactly
where the model has no basis to predict. Attaching an IC50 to them would
be inventing a number.

What the evidence supports: they are novel against the curated ChEMBL
set, synthetically plausible by SAscore, free of PAINS alerts, and they
occupy the BACE1 site about as well as known inhibitors do in the same
receptor and box.

That is a shortlist worth a chemist's hour. It is not a result, and the
only way to find out whether any of them bind is to make them and test
them.

Written to runs/shortlist.json
